# Research

Discovery chooses evidence; `best-api` decides call shape and the Plan playbook
owns adoption. Research does not silently patch runtime or become Benchmark.
Issue-by-issue closure belongs to `issue-harvester`.

1. Read current compiled knowledge under `docs/research`, its schema, matching
   plans and relevant lessons under `docs/solutions`. State the question, bounded scope, current gap, exclusions,
   stop condition and eventual proof owner before searching.
2. Before declaring a corpus missing, check its official entrypoints and the
   strongest matching local evidence. Distinguish searched paths from files
   actually read. Use primary docs and local source checkouts. Record exact repository
   revisions and licenses. Search results and READMEs are leads; inspect real
   code before a code-level claim. Reuse a fresh prior read when its question,
   revision and dependencies still match.
3. Keep query, lead, read, rejected and promotion rows under a dated research
   run. Record source path/revision, inspected spans, claim, evidence grade,
   applicability, proof owner and next action. Keep bulk raw corpora outside
   compiled pages; parse ledgers by exact header names.
4. Grade local inspected source with runnable proof highest. Detailed upstream
   reports can suggest an invariant. Secondary pages and snippets only choose
   the next read. Prefer tests, oracles and measurement methods over speculative
   runtime rewrites.
5. Promote one test, benchmark, plan, docs or no-code packet with its owner and
   verification command. Keep rejected leads with their reopening condition.

`audit` inventories every file in the explicitly bounded owner before making
an exhaustive comparison. Name each file read, its revision, the behavior it
carries, the Plate/Slate owner and keep/adapt/reject decision. An unread member
is a gap, not inferred coverage. `audit sync` refreshes recorded audits at new
revisions and reopens only affected claims.

`harvest` inventories upstream behavior evidence and existing local coverage.
Express the invariant independently after the license gate. Never copy fixture
or helper shape as a substitute for understanding. `harvest plan` maps each
accepted row to its current Plate or upstream Slate owner, adoption step and
exact proof. Runtime implementation needs separate active authority.

`maintain` repairs stale claims, contradictions, duplication, broken links and
orphan knowledge from evidence. Before retiring an internal document, move
each still-true lesson into a named home a workflow reads. `full` accounts for
every scoped corpus as evidenced or a named raw, compile, synthesis,
freshness, evidence or contradiction gap. A spot check cannot claim full.

Keep reusable summaries and decisions in `docs/research`; keep temporary
observations in the run. Do not treat a summary as stronger than its source.
Unresolved gaps name their owner and the evidence or condition that closes
them. Report sources actually read, promoted/rejected leads, proof limits and
the next shard. Preserve historical ledger schemas and manual decisions.
